1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,152
What happens when the processing center goes completely silent?

2
00:00:04,202 --> 00:00:11,016
A debit with no answer is unknown: the money may have moved, so it is never declined, and never sent again.

3
00:00:11,066 --> 00:00:16,848
Someone has to ask the scheme later, and keep asking, even if the app restarts in between.

4
00:00:16,898 --> 00:00:22,584
So each unknown debit gets a Temporal workflow, and Temporal keeps its waits durable.

5
00:00:22,634 --> 00:00:30,720
The workflow waits, asks the scheme, and waits longer each time: thirty seconds, then one minute, two, and up to ten.

6
00:00:30,770 --> 00:00:40,800
It asks with the same reference the debit carried, our payment id, so the answer is about this debit and nothing else, and a Humo hold still waiting is captured then.

7
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:46,872
Approved makes the payment paid, declined makes it declined, and the journal records the answer.

8
00:00:46,922 --> 00:00:52,704
After twenty four hours with no answer, a person decides: the payment goes to manual review.

9
00:00:52,754 --> 00:00:57,432
The workflow's id is the payment's, so starting it twice keeps the first.

10
00:00:57,482 --> 00:01:03,936
A sweep every minute starts it for anything left unknown, and for debits the app stopped in the middle of.

11
00:01:03,986 --> 00:01:10,872
If Temporal itself is down, the debit still ends unknown, and the next sweep starts the workflow.

12
00:01:10,922 --> 00:01:15,960
The buyer's page keeps checking, and turns paid when the scheme finally answers.

13
00:01:16,010 --> 00:01:19,008
The dashboard counts how unknown debits ended.

14
00:01:19,058 --> 00:01:24,360
Next, telling the merchant what happened, reliably: the outbox and Kafka.
